---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TalkBanner from '../components/TalkBanner.astro';
import LegalDoc from '../components/LegalDoc.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { withBase } from '../config/paths';

// Checked 2026-10-27: no Set-Cookie on any page or the enquiry endpoint, and no localStorage,
// sessionStorage or document.cookie anywhere in src/. Recheck before adding any script or embed.
---

<BaseLayout page="cookies">
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />

  <LegalDoc title="Cookie policy" updated="27 October 2026">
    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>
      This website sets no cookies. It runs no analytics, advertising or tracking, and it stores
      nothing in your browser. That is why there is no cookie banner.
    </p>

    <h2>What cookies are</h2>
    <p>
      Cookies are small files a website saves in your browser. Some are needed for a site to work,
      such as keeping you signed in. Others track what you do, often for analytics or advertising.
      Similar tools, such as local storage, work in much the same way, and this policy covers them
      too.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies on this site</h2>
    <p>
      None. We don't set cookies on any page, on the contact form or on the free AI check form, and
      we don't use local storage or similar tools. The site's fonts, images and videos are all
      served from our own domain, so no other company's content loads when you visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Security cookies from our host</h2>
    <p>
      The site is hosted by Cloudflare. If Cloudflare's protection ever needs to check whether a
      visitor is a person or a bot, it may set a strictly necessary security cookie, such as
      <code>__cf_bm</code> or <code>cf_clearance</code>. These cookies are used only to protect the
      site. They don't track you across other websites, and they last no more than the time the
      check needs. Under the UK's Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations (PECR), cookies
      that are strictly necessary to protect a service don't need consent.
    </p>

    <h2>When you leave this site</h2>
    <p>
      Links to Instagram, Google and other websites take you to services with their own cookie and
      privacy policies. Those apply once you are on their sites.
    </p>

    <h2>If this changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we ever add analytics or any other cookies, we will update this policy first and ask for
      your consent wherever the law requires it.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a>. How we handle
      information you send us is in our <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>privacy notice</a>.
    </p>
  </LegalDoc>

  <TalkBanner />

  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
